<title>USA: April Brent dips in thin late U.S. trading.</title>
<headline>April Brent dips in thin late U.S. trading.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bellwether North Sea Brent dipped in thin late U.S. trading on Tuesday, with only a few players participating, traders said.</p>
<p>Four partial paper April Brents changed hands a total of 350 times at $20.75, $20.68 and $20.67 a barrel. London's IPE settled at $20.75.</p>
<p>March/April Brent moved at 40 cents, up one cent from the London close.</p>
<p>--Patricia Garip-Bertuol NY Energy Desk ((+1 212 859 1620))</p>
</text>
